# Replay desk contract

Extend ADR 017's canonical history engine; ADR 001/003/005 govern module extraction
and ADR 006 governs feature CSS. Capture remains a compatibility feeder.

- Capture reproducible baseline measurements before changing hot paths; report the
  fixture, sample count, runtime, before/after latency and measurement limitations.
- Share historical snapshot/status polling across consumers, permit only one request
  per resource, cancel obsolete work, retain same-playhead data on transient failure,
  and invalidate immediately on seek to prevent future-print flashes.
- Shared chart bars own one internal AbortController per symbol/timeframe. Seek
  invalidation cancels the obsolete network request as well as its generation;
  aborting one consumer must never cancel another consumer's shared request.
- Render persistent truthful download progress from durable cursor/time fields.
  ETA is an estimate, absent without progress; stalled/failed jobs remain visible.
- Serialize session-clock, capture-selection and historical-selection mutations across
  controls. An explicit wall-follow or source selection cancels any debounced or
  queued seek intent, then runs after the already-sent mutation settles.
- Keep independent actions usable, bound requests, expose errors without JSON parser
  gibberish, restore focus on close, and respect symbol/module layout preferences.
- Use feature-layer CSS and existing tokens in both themes; preserve virtualized tape.
- No disk I/O in async handlers or repeated selection-wide work under the playback
  lock on every poll. Cache only with explicit selection/time/data invalidation;
  no lookahead, identical prints/order and reported-volume semantics must survive.
- Empty historical tick pages before the end refuse resumably with unchanged cursor;
  never infer complete coverage or synthesize prints from an empty response.
- Persist integer capture schema_version; migrate known unversioned legacy rows or refuse unknown
  formats. Surface malformed/dropped-row counts and decimation rather than hiding it.
- Coalesce pending L2 and flush its final state; reject backwards capture timestamps.
  Daily bars are emitted at rollover/flush, not per print. Default capture paths stay
  outside the repository. Do not add auto-pruning or choose retention policy (#320).
- Retention, IBKR candle presentation (#304), replay depth/quotes and practice orders
  remain separate decisions. No execution gate changes or live trading operations.
